<title>DUBAI: Dubai gold imports hit record 350.49 T in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dubai gold imports hit record 350.49 T in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold imports into Dubai, a major trading centre for the precious metal, surged to a record 350.49 tonnes in 1996 from 318.03 tonnes in 1995, the World Gold Council (WGC) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In 1994, the emirate imported 257.1 tonnes.</p>
<p>Most of Dubai's gold imports go on to the Indian subcontinent and particularly India -- the world's single largest market.</p>
<p>The WGC is a non-profit association owned by major gold producers and monitors about 75 percent of the world's markets.</p>
</text>
